SUMMARY:Sunday Leisure Walk (BuskerFest Festival—Walk\, Talk and Have Fu
 n!)
DESCRIPTION:Soul City Social Club (Toronto\, Canada)\nHello everyone\,\n\n
 \\*Please read carefully\\*\n\nGet ready for an afternoon filled with laug
 hter\, amazing street performances and new friendships at the Toronto Inte
 rnational BuskerFest! We’ll walk through the festival together\, enjoy t
 he sights and sounds\, and take in some of the most creative and entertain
 ing performers Toronto has to offer.\n\\*Many of us will probably head dow
 n to the Beaches Boardwalk and/or Queen Street too for more site seeing\, 
 ice cream and find a nice place for dinner and beverages after\n\n\\*Joine
 d by my other groups too :)\n\n**Arrive between 4:00 pm and 4:30 pm**\n\n*
 *Where to meet us:**\n\nMeetup us outside **Woodbine Station beside bike r
 acks**\n**The Main Woodbine Station Entrance:** Located at the southeast c
 orner of Woodbine Avenue and Strathmore Boulevard.\n\nWe will walk as a gr
 oup from the station down to Ashbridges Bay\n\\*Most will stick around aft
 er for a bite to eat and a beverage to sip on :)\n\nFurther details below:
 \n\nSincerely\,\n\nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details:**\
 n**Sunday Leisure Walk (The Toronto International BuskerFest Festival—Wa
 lk\, Talk and Have Fun!)**\n\nWhat to expect:\n\n* A relaxed walk together
  along Woodbine to the BuskerFest Festival\n* Ice breaker games to get to 
 know one another\n* Plenty of opportunities to mix\, mingle and meet new p
 eople\n* A comfortable pace that allows everyone to walk and talk\n* Beaut
 iful views of the lake\, beach\, parkland and surrounding area during and 
 after BuskerFest\n* A positive atmosphere for both newcomers and returning
  members\n\nPlease wear comfortable walking shoes and bring water\, sunscr
 een or anything else you may need for the weather. The purpose of this eve
 nt is simple: get outside\, enjoy the day and make a few new connections!\
 n\n{Optional Read: **More about BuskerFest}**\nFrom musicians and jugglers
  to acrobats\, comedians and living statues\, BuskerFest offers something 
 unexpected around every corner. This outing is a wonderful opportunity to 
 explore the festival at a relaxed pace while talking\, laughing and connec
 ting with other friendly folks. Come by yourself or bring a friend—our f
 ocus is simply to have fun\, enjoy the performances\, see other parts the 
 water front and make everyone feel welcome.\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**Event Fee:**\n10 dollars
  (cash only) when you arrive (HST is included)\nor e transfer in advance t
 o [Steveflemming11@gmail.com](mailto:Steveflemming11@gmail.com)\n\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\n(Optional to support the festival once we arrive-extra cost:\n**Ad
 mission**: **By donation** at the gate (a suggested donation of $5 to $10 
 per person benefiting [Epilepsy Toronto](https://epilepsytoronto.org/about
 -us/events/toronto-international-buskerfest-for-epilepsy/). Tip your stree
 t performers separately if you enjoy their acts!\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\nParking near Woodbine Sta
 tion:\n(Although I encourage you to take subway if you can)
